WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
bokura nara daijoubu

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
Because we’re still doing okay,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
we can become even stronger!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
takaihiroi sora megake

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
Aiming for the tall and wide sky,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
kinou made no boku wo hanatsu

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
I let go of what I was up until yesterday.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
miesuita uso mo, taikutsu na

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
Those lies that were easily seen through and my tedious day-by-day life;

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
hibi mo, zenbu hodoite

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
I left them both behind.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
atarashii asa ni me wo hosome

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
I narrowed my eyes at the new morning

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
kyou mo bokutachi wa ikiteku

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
Today we shall also venture out
to live our lives again.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
sukoshi nami utsu sabishisadatte

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
Even the slight loneliness that sometimes comes about,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
taisetsu ni omoeteru

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
I consider important.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
itsuka kanjita shinjitsu mo

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
Even the truth I felt some day…

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
massugu koko kara asu ni mukatteru

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
…is urging us to go on into the future.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
bokutachi ga mezashita sekai

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
The world that we had all aimed for…

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
donna kakomo kakaeta mama kitto tadoritsuku

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
We will arrive at it, no matter what our pasts are.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
fumidashita kewashii michi mo

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.460
We continued forward, even if it is a steep path…

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
bokura nara daijoubu,

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:11.900
…because we’re still doing okay,

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
and we can become even stronger!

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.550
I’m off!

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:46.750
Wait, Onii-chan!

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.940
YAY! We’ve got you!

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:55.490
Don’t just leave us behind!

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:00.370
Billy!

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:04.580
I see!

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:07.960
Billy feels lonely without Onii-chan!

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.870
He really likes Onii-chan!

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:17.470
Don’t do that, Billy!

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.630
You two can play together
when we get back!

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:21.410
Be a good kid and
watch the house, okay?

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.750
Let’s skip!

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.210
Yeah, let’s skip!

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.780
We’ll see you later, Onii-chan!

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:45.120
Hurry up and come back!

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:47.040
We’re waiting to bake cookies for you.

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.060
See ya!

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:49.460
Okay!

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:52.460
Don’t cheat on us!

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.170
How could I be cheating?

00:03:02.390 --> 00:03:04.140
Good morning, Nozomu-kun!

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:07.470
Fancy our meeting here…
what an incredible coincidence!

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.190
This must be destiny!

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:11.940
It must be destiny!

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.230
We’re just taking the same
path to school…

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:16.070
Kenmochi-san, we’ll get off here!

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:18.590
Yes, but…

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:22.320
It’s okay. We’ve almost reached school.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.640
All right. Be careful.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.330
Good morning, Nozomu-kun.

00:03:28.830 --> 00:03:30.100
Ah, good morning.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:33.880
Thank you very much for helping us last time at the department store.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.070
What you taught us really helped!

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:38.700
Oh, it’s nothing.

00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:41.220
It we hadn’t met you that time…

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.590
what would we have done?

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.680
Huh? What is it?

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:51.520
So this is what it’s like to walk to school with a guy!

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:53.650
Yeah, yeah!

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:56.870
This is something we’ve been longing for, right?

00:03:56.870 --> 00:03:59.980
To walk to school with a guy as a threesome…

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.030
It would’ve been unthinkable when we were at the girls’ school!

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:09.540
I’m nervous.

00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:10.520
I’m excited.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:13.230
But it’s a bit embarrassing somehow.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:16.730
Perhaps it’s a little early for us to be doing this…

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.880
Please do this again next time!

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:26.390
What the…?

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:42.740
Good morning!

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.110
Hey there!

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:46.200
Nozomu-chan, have you gotten used to this school yet?

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:47.600
Are you in any sort of trouble?

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:51.940
No, since everyone has been so kind to me. I’m doing okay.

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.040
Is that so? I’m glad.

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:56.370
We were worried about you.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:00.630
We wondered if you would break down and start crying.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.630
Yeah, since you used to be a crybaby!

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:04.450
W-Was I?

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:07.390
Not!

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:10.560
It would have been better if we had been in the same class.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.250
We could have given you more help.

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:17.310
Am I being attractive?

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:25.200
“We could have given you more help,” Nozomu-chan?

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:27.930
No, it was just…

00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:30.660
Ah, it’s Gonda-kun and the others!

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:33.600
Wow… you’ve already made friends with them? Incredible!

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:37.170
Of course. Right, Futami-kun?

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:39.130
Yeah.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:41.000
I’m glad, Nozomu-chan.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.340
Please take care of Nozomu-chan, guys.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.670
Okay!

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.900
What? Why are you sighing?

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:03.270
After all, you were getting lots of attention this morning.

00:06:03.270 --> 00:06:05.690
Do you think that was
“getting lots of attention”?

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.240
Of course it was!

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:09.490
By very cute girls!

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:13.450
On top of that, you got lots of attention from 3 sets of twins!

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:14.700
What could you complain about?

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:16.690
Is that so?

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:21.210
Are you sure?

00:06:22.460 --> 00:06:24.800
Well… be careful.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:25.550
Eh?

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:29.180
Haven’t you heard about the legend of the grave of the twins?

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:32.870
If you let yourself get carried away,
you might get the curse of the grave!

00:06:33.510 --> 00:06:35.270
Curse?

00:06:37.850 --> 00:06:41.690
Oh yes, we’ll have elective classes this afternoon.

00:06:41.690 --> 00:06:44.710
Futami-kun, Sakurazuki Kira-san and Yura-san,

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.510
have you all decided which class you want to attend?

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:49.600
Ah, I’ll be doing Engineering.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:52.990
Oh my, we haven’t decided yet.

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:55.330
What should we do?
Which would be good?

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:57.500
Umm… umm…

00:06:57.500 --> 00:06:59.330
What should we do, Yura-chan?

00:06:59.330 --> 00:07:01.040
Umm… umm…

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:03.040
This is troublesome, Kira-chan.

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.340
Ah, you don’t have to make a decision right now.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:07.260
Take your time to think about it.

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:10.260
I’m in charge of the home economics class, by the way.

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.870
Today, we’ll be making tasty apple pie!

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:15.120
Apple pie?

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:19.620
Hey, wasn’t there something
like that in Papa’s ordeal #7?

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:21.940
To cook food!

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:25.400
Let’s choose home economics for our elective class!

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:26.690
Yeah!

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:32.610
Hey, umm… how about…

00:07:32.610 --> 00:07:34.160
Yura-chan! That’s a great idea!

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:37.270
Nozomu-kun?

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:38.120
Hmm?

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:40.660
Do you like apple pie, Nozomu-kun?

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.250
Eh? Yeah, I like it.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:49.010
We’re going to make apple pie
in this afternoon’s class.

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:50.720
Please taste it…

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:54.220
Since it’s for Nozomu-kun, we’ll do our best even if we die trying!

00:07:54.220 --> 00:07:56.790
Yeah. Umm… “die”?

00:07:57.390 --> 00:08:01.810
It’s such a dream to make
a snack for a guy!

00:08:01.810 --> 00:08:03.730
Finally, the dream will come true!

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:07.300
We can return the favor to Nozomu-chan, so it’s great, Yura-chan!

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:15.120
Wh-What did you say?

00:08:15.120 --> 00:08:18.330
The Misses are going to make apple pie?

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.850
I can’t believe it!

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:19.850
Yes.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:22.330
It is one of Master’s ordeals.

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:25.130
Even though cooking is one of the master’s ordeals…

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:30.840
the Misses have never used a kitchen knife, scissors, or even a nail clipper before!

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:31.760
Yes, yes!

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:37.350
How incredible, the misses’ spirit of challenge!

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:39.850
I am so moved!

00:08:39.850 --> 00:08:40.960
Actually, Kenmochi-sama…

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:43.770
Hmm? Apple pie…

00:08:43.770 --> 00:08:45.770
For that “Nozomu-kun” boy?

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:56.720
Ah, Nozomu-chan!

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:01.290
Perfect timing! I was talking with Sumireko, and…

00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:02.650
Hey, the Ichijou twins!

00:09:04.210 --> 00:09:05.920
Ah, Kosaka-kun!

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:09.290
Ah, I see. You’re in the same class as Nozomu-chan!

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:11.300
It’s so nostalgic…

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:16.430
Me and Nozomu-kun used to play with you guys a lot!

00:09:16.430 --> 00:09:17.720
Since we were at
the same kindergarten,

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:20.810
the four of us would play hide and seek together at Nekojarashi Park!

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:25.500
It’s okay if you don’t remember.

00:09:26.020 --> 00:09:29.440
Oh no, it’s not that we don’t remember…

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:30.150
Yeah, yeah!

00:09:31.070 --> 00:09:32.360
Is that so?

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:35.600
So, what was that about
“perfect timing”?

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:37.610
Ah, yes.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:41.450
Umm… we’re going to make an apple pie
in home economics class.

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:43.440
Do you like apple pie, Nozomu-chan?

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.270
Yeah, I like it.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:47.420
Ah, I’m so relieved!

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:51.020
I think I’ll be making it for you.

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:52.110
Me too!

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:56.590
When I try cooking for someone,
I feel like I can do better.

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:01.510
Kosaka-kun, if it’s okay with you,
please have some.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:02.160
You can have some.

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:04.370
WITH PLEASURE!!!

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:08.650
Oh no! We have to go early to prepare.

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:10.360
Yes! We need to hurry!

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:12.610
Please look forward to it!

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:13.530
Yippee!

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:18.860
I can’t believe I get to eat
an apple pie made by a girl…

00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:20.030
It’s like a dream.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:22.740
I’ve waited so long for this day!

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:26.450
Hey, you said you’re going to eat the one the Sakurazuki twins make, right?

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:28.620
Yeah, that’s right.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.130
You can’t eat everything, right?

00:10:30.130 --> 00:10:32.920
Leave it to me! I’ll help you finish it!

00:10:32.920 --> 00:10:35.810
A portion of what the Ichijou twins make… a portion of what the Sakurazuki twins make…

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:51.980
Is everyone ready?

00:10:53.020 --> 00:10:55.000
Let’s make some tasty apple pies, okay?

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:56.800
Okay!

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:02.380
So you two have decided to take the home economics class?

00:11:02.380 --> 00:11:03.280
Yes!

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:06.080
But this is our first time cooking.

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:07.520
I’m worried if we could do it well…

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:09.370
You’ll be fine.

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:12.380
That’s what you’ll be learning in this class.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:15.400
Okay, everyone! Let’s begin by checking our ingredients!

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:24.160
Do your best, misses.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:31.470
Handmade apple pie…
it must be really tasty!

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:33.900
I want to hurry up and eat it!

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:38.000
So what are we doing in Engineering?

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.160
Rice planting?

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:47.120
It just happens that we’re doing this today.

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:49.250
No one told me about this.

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:50.580
Also…

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:53.250
Gosh, this is a joint class?!

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:56.540
He seems to be in a bad mood…

00:11:57.050 --> 00:11:59.050
What in the world did I do?

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:01.490
Something to incur the wrath of the Ichijou Fan Club?

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:06.570
I think I’ll be making it for you.

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:07.450
Me too!

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:09.700
Apple pie…

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:13.190
So, everyone! Planting rice requires physical strength.

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:15.210
First, we’ll begin with warm-up exercises.

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:20.970
Okay… 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8….

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:26.950
2, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8…

00:12:27.280 --> 00:12:32.330
3, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8…

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:33.830
What’s with the random movements?

00:12:32.950 --> 00:12:38.110
4, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8…

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.480
Ah, I expected no less from the Ichijou sisters.

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:43.660
You’re making it really well.

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:47.110
We’ve made apple pie before.

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:49.240
Also, we have a reason
for working hard at it.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.670
Oh my… what is it?

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:54.240
It’s a secret!

00:12:54.240 --> 00:12:55.300
A secret! A secret!

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.410
Oh well…

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:03.250
Oh yes, get the cinnamon from the cabinet, okay?

00:13:03.250 --> 00:13:04.260
Okay!

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:15.060
Sakurazuki-san…

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:16.350
Yes?

00:13:16.350 --> 00:13:20.230
It’s so fun to make pie dough!

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:24.060
But the flour flies out, so it’s a difficult task.

00:13:27.320 --> 00:13:30.570
Kira-san, Yura-san…
did you add water?

00:13:30.570 --> 00:13:32.280
Eh? Water?

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:34.080
Ah, I forgot.

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.580
If you don’t add water, you see…

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:42.960
I can’t believe the Misses, who have never played with mud, are kneading udon-ko…

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:42.960
Note: They were using <i>udon-ko</i>, flour for making udon noodles, instead of <i>merikenko</i>

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:47.010
<i>Merikenko</i> (American-style flour) is flour usually used to make pie crusts.

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:44.790
It’s incredible!

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:47.010
This Kenmochi is so moved by it!

00:13:49.130 --> 00:13:49.850
Umm…

00:13:54.760 --> 00:13:56.560
What are you doing?

00:13:56.560 --> 00:14:00.230
Ah, sorry about that. I was engrossed with something else.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:01.110
It was accidental.

00:14:01.810 --> 00:14:02.850
Accidental?

00:14:07.320 --> 00:14:09.990
Kosaka is incredible.
He must be a specialist.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:16.240
Manual labor is fun, isn’t it, sensei?

00:14:16.240 --> 00:14:18.290
Plus, I’m feeling pretty hungry right now.

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:22.500
I feel alive!

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:24.180
Hey, Kosaka!

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:25.910
That guy…

00:14:26.790 --> 00:14:29.920
That poor fellow…
he won’t be able to eat apple pie.

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:30.850
Why?

00:14:31.590 --> 00:14:34.310
You and Kosaka-kun really hate apple pie, right?

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:41.810
Right? Right? You hate it, right?
RIGHT? Right?! RIGHT!!!?

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.410
What is going on?

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:49.940
Nothing! We were just playing around!

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:52.280
Sorry. It was an accident.

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:53.570
Are you okay, Futami?

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:57.570
Yeah, I guess it’s okay.
It can’t be helped.

00:14:57.570 --> 00:14:58.800
Futami! Go wash up.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:00.410
Okay!

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:07.500
What is it with those guys?

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:10.800
They’re misunderstanding my relationship with Kaoruko and Sumireko.

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:12.630
Misunderstanding…

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:13.590
Misunderstanding?

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:20.510
If they really did like me, I’d understand why Gonda and the others are angry.

00:15:22.180 --> 00:15:23.990
What am I thinking?

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:41.440
It went well!

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:41.920
Yeah!

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:46.270
So I’m getting that.
I’m really fortunate…

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:55.800
Yura-chan, you have flour on your nose.

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:05.020
Kira-chan and Yura-chan are also working hard for me.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:06.930
Maybe I’m fortunate…

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:17.780
President!

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:18.290
Huh?

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:20.290
It’s bad!

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:21.780
WHAT?!?

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:23.580
Futami was watching the cooking class?

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:27.830
That’s why he didn’t come back…

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.000
This is unforgivable! Let’s go!

00:16:32.750 --> 00:16:33.430
What’s going on?

00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.300
What is it with those guys?

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:40.260
Something smells good.

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:43.100
I think the girls are cooking something.

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.690
It seems to be apple pie today.

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:47.310
I want to eat some!

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:48.530
Let’s go!

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:51.650
Hey, wait! Wait!

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:58.780
What is it with everyone?

00:16:58.780 --> 00:17:02.020
All the guys are more interested
in apple pie.

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:04.730
Ah, over there…

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:12.280
The apple pie they’re baking for me looks like it’s almost done!

00:17:12.280 --> 00:17:15.040
Hey, is it okay not to go back?

00:17:15.040 --> 00:17:17.390
Sensei is over here, too.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:26.510
The Misses’ first handmade apple pie…

00:17:27.170 --> 00:17:30.890
The only people who have the right to eat it are the Master…

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:34.850
and this Kenmochi, who have watched the Misses grow since childhood!

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:40.470
We will not give it to that Nozomu-kun boy who popped up out of nowhere!

00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:43.210
Doesn’t it smell like something burning?

00:17:43.970 --> 00:17:44.900
Really!

00:17:44.900 --> 00:17:45.500
What’s going on?

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:51.550
Oh no!

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:52.870
Look out, Misses!

00:17:57.330 --> 00:17:58.250
What is it?

00:18:01.120 --> 00:18:03.180
Are you okay, you two?

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:09.550
It has fragrance and delicacy!

00:18:09.550 --> 00:18:11.760
The first apple pie!

00:18:11.760 --> 00:18:13.680
I have tasted it!

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:15.100
Kenmochi-san!

00:18:17.260 --> 00:18:22.030
I’m so happy, Misses…

00:18:25.940 --> 00:18:27.250
Here you go!

00:18:29.070 --> 00:18:31.340
How many times
have I dreamt about this?

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:34.910
It’s nice that the Ichijou twins baked their pie well.

00:18:34.910 --> 00:18:37.330
We’ve failed.

00:18:37.330 --> 00:18:41.080
I thought the pie for
Nozomu-kun was gone.

00:18:41.080 --> 00:18:42.670
But this looks so tasty…

00:18:42.670 --> 00:18:44.830
I have full confidence
in how we made it!

00:18:44.830 --> 00:18:46.230
Please try it.

00:18:46.630 --> 00:18:48.670
It’s really good!

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:50.460
Okay, I’m digging in!

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:56.110
Huh? This scent…

00:18:57.600 --> 00:18:59.520
This scent that pierces the nose…

00:19:00.310 --> 00:19:01.730
I’ve smelt it somewhere else…

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:07.370
This is… sansho!

00:19:05.400 --> 00:19:08.580
Note: Sansho is a pepper made from the seeds of the Japanese prickly ash

00:19:10.650 --> 00:19:11.940
You’re right!

00:19:11.940 --> 00:19:12.710
No way!

00:19:14.360 --> 00:19:18.130
Ah! We must have grabbed the wrong one from the spice cabinet!

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:23.820
It doesn’t seem so tasty now…

00:19:24.250 --> 00:19:26.130
I don’t think so!

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:27.710
Maybe sansho works out fine.

00:19:28.090 --> 00:19:29.000
NO!

00:19:29.000 --> 00:19:32.550
We can’t let Nozomu-chan eat a failed product!

00:19:32.550 --> 00:19:33.400
But…

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:37.010
We’ll make it again for you another day;
you can eat it then.

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:40.970
Next time, it will definitely be tasty! Right, Kaoruko?

00:19:40.970 --> 00:19:42.300
Yeah, Sumireko!

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:45.520
We’ll definitely try our best as well…
right, Yura-chan?

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:48.410
Yes, Kira-chan!
We’ll have him eat it next time.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:52.770
See you later, Nozomu-chan!

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:56.780
Hold it!

00:19:57.450 --> 00:19:58.480
I’ll dispose of that.

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:07.520
Okay, everyone…
let’s eat this with gratitude.

00:20:14.800 --> 00:20:17.180
We’ll never forget this taste!

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:18.330
It’s the taste of love…

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:29.040
Ah, it looks good!

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:31.580
Onii-chan will definitely be happy!

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:32.860
I’m back!

00:20:32.860 --> 00:20:33.990
It’s Onii-chan!

00:20:35.570 --> 00:20:37.410
Onii-chan!

00:20:37.410 --> 00:20:38.170
Hmm?

00:20:40.660 --> 00:20:42.920
What is it, Ruru-chan, Rara-chan?

00:20:43.450 --> 00:20:44.370
Here you go!

00:20:44.370 --> 00:20:45.160
What is it?

00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:47.620
It’s what we’ve baked for you.

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:49.380
Savour the taste as you eat!

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:51.390
Oh yeah… this morning…

00:21:17.740 --> 00:21:21.410
In the end, I didn’t get
to eat pie or cookies.

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:27.420
Maybe it’s the curse of the grave of the twins…

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:32.900
However, everyone did their best making them for me.

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:36.180
Maybe this is something
to be happy about.

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
dokomademo tsuzuku sora

00:21:52.000 --> 00:21:58.000
Oh, the sky that continues no matter where you go…

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
daisuki na kono machi de

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:04.050
In this town that I love…

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.010
takusan no omoide to, hora,

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.010
With all our memories, now look!

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:16.020
onaji dake hohoende

00:22:10.010 --> 00:22:16.020
We are smiling the same way

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:26.700
itsudemo kimi no tonari ni iyoutoshiteru no wa

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:26.700
To always be trying to be besides you…

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
mukashi kara no kuse datte omotteru kedo

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
…is, I believe, a bad habit I’ve had for a long time

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
“mata ashita” tte te wo furu toki ni wa

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
When we wave our hands saying “see you tomorrow,”

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
sukoshi dake samishii kigasuru yo

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
I realize that I’m feeling a little lonely at that moment

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
tooku naru kimi no senaka mitsumete

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
Staring at your back that is getting further away,

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
nandaka, fushigi na kimochi

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
For some reason, a mysterious feeling…

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
kono mune ni hirogatte yuku

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
…is spreading through this heart of mine

00:23:10.560 --> 00:23:12.490
This is Kenmochi.

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:16.650
In this town, there is a place called the Chigusa Veterinarian Hospital.

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:21.000
And Kira-sama and Yura-sama…
Oh no, I have to stop there.
